I walk over to the front desk.
A volunteer stands behind the desk.
He smiles and says hello.
"Welcome to the club," he says.
"Thank you," I answer.
"I want to do sports," I say.
"That is a good idea," he says.
"What is your name?" he asks.
"My name is Maya," I answer.
He registers my name on a computer.
"Do you have a racket?" he asks.
"No, I do not have a racket," I say.
"You can rent a racket here," he says.
"It costs fifty kroner."
I pay fifty kroner.
He gives me a green racket.
"I really like to play badminton," I say.
"It is also very fun," he smiles.
"You can play on court number three," he says.
I walk over to court number three.
